# What `docker build -f image/Dockerfile .` sends to the builder: the files the image reads, and
# nothing else (STD-GLB-009 §Container Images rule 12, ADR-GLB-020).
#
# Docker: "the files and directories that match patterns in the files are removed from the build
# context before it's sent to the builder" (Build context, docs.docker.com). A file that is never
# sent can neither be copied into a layer nor fail the build because the builder cannot read it.
#
# The Dockerfile copies themes/scnehaux and image/start.sh. Neither is below.

# Secrets and key material: the realm keystore under deploy/dev/keys, a stack's .env, a server's
# Compose override, a stray private key and a local token.
**/keys/
.env
**/.env
*.pem
**/*.pem
**/compose.override.yaml
.token

# Local state: sibling checkouts a workflow places here, proof and scan working directories, test
# and build output.
.kernel/
.identity/
.experience/
.image-scan/
.dockerignore-check.*
coverage
cov-src
*.out
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Version control and CI metadata: never read by the build.
.git
.github
